{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/7973-brazilian-portuguese-terms","id":7973,"title":"Brazilian Portuguese terms","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-11-11T04:30:57-08:00","id":7973,"title":"Brazilian Portuguese terms","content":"Hello developers. :-]<br /> <br /> Since the Trinity Continuum will come back, I'd REALLY like to ask you something: please, take some care with Brazilian Portuguese.<br /> <br /> Brazil is an important country in Trinity, and I really was taken &quot;off-guard&quot; when I saw that in the original book (my friends were also surprised), but we all noticed that the &quot;BR-portuguese&quot; you used was not quite...right.<br /> <br /> So, if you can, please, take at least a little &quot;consulting&quot; with a Native Brazilian that uses the language frequently. This way, the final terms within the book, and their use, will sound &quot;right&quot; to our ears. by doing so, you gain 1) verisimilitude and 2) a bigger possible pool of players (many Brazilian friends of mine just went insane when I told them that they could play with Brazilians and that would affect how their characters are perceived in-world).<br /> <br /> Thank you. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1001-timecrafter","name":"Timecrafter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1001_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-11T05:16:29-08:00","id":7985,"title":"","content":"Like MOST Brazilians, I can't speak Spanish (which may sound weird for you since I can read English perfectly). Because of that, I can tell you that some terms sound REALLY weird to us, or DO NOT EVEN EXIST in Portuguese. Now that it's clear, please notice that my suggestions only deal with BR-Portuguese terms; I cannot say anything about the Spanish ones.<br /> <br /> My very first suggestion: <br /> <br /> &quot;Orgulho de C\u00e9u&quot; HURTS our ears <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />. Really.<br /> please, change this to &quot;Orgulho do C\u00e9u&quot; or even better &quot;Orgulho Celeste&quot;.<br /> <br /> Take note of these: asesino de la moto, desechables, wakina sisi. THESE TERMS DO NOT EXIST. Sorry to tell you that, pal; if these words do exist, they ARE NOT Portuguese. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> Oh, and there are others in the &quot;non-existent&quot; list. :-[<br /> <br /> When in Brazil, change &quot;Pai de Nor\u00e7a&quot; to &quot;Pai da Nor\u00e7a&quot;. And translate &quot;Nor\u00e7a&quot;'s meaning to &quot;Nova For\u00e7a Nacional&quot; when used by Brazilians.<br /> <br /> Finally, to many Brazilians, &quot;Giuseppe del Fuego&quot; is an awkward name to remember and utter correctly. And most important: it's not exactly <i>difficult</i>... but it always sounds &quot;alien&quot;. It screams &quot;I'm not form here&quot;, or &quot;I'm from Mexico&quot;, or at most, &quot;I'm Argentinian or from other South American Country&quot;. For a Brazilian, it doesn't feel like a member of the group, much less a a brother, even less a Father. And following the Plot, Giuseppe would <i>never </i>let that happen. So, my suggestion is: whenever the Proxy deals with Portuguese-speaking nations, his pseudonym should be &quot;Z\u00e9 do Fogo&quot;. That one sounds &quot;right&quot; to us: to Brazilian ears, even in the countryside (or, specially in the countryside ) it screams, at the same time: &quot;badass&quot; and &quot;one of us&quot;. You feel this guy like a &quot;brother in arms&quot; and one which can stand his ground. The best <i>literal </i>translation I can give is &quot;Joe from Fire&quot; or &quot;Joe which has Fire&quot;, but believe me, that SOUNDS Brazilian, and fits the image the Proxy builds for himself. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1001-timecrafter","name":"Timecrafter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1001_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-11T06:49:36-08:00","id":8027,"title":"","content":"Previous books established that by the 2120s, Brazil uses &quot;Portu\u00f1ol,&quot; a fusion of Portuguese and Spanish. Accordingly a lot of terms that don't sound right in strict Portuguese would sound fine in Portu\u00f1ol. Guiseppe del Fuego was always a pseudonym anyway, and not his real name.<br /> <br /> There's no guarantee that anything -- terminology, proxies, orders -- will be exactly the same as in the previous edition. In fact odds are they won't be. However, John very much wants accuracy across the board. We've already stated that Nor\u00e7a won't be a shortening of what it used to be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}